+\subsection{Execution Audits and Retained Validation Failures}
+\label{sec:native-audit}
+All 640 new runs pass the declared execution audit and independent detection
+and policy replay. Raw packet events reconstruct receiver P10/counts and
+canary retransmissions; ACK and physical-leg events reconstruct remaining
+work, route measurements, health-report delivery and policy arithmetic.
+All 640 retained raw archives have verified SHA-256 digests, and frozen
+scoring regenerates the retained trial and pair tables. These checks verify
+recorded content and modeled invariants, not every job's completion.
+
+In the main four benefit-policy cohorts (240 trials), 180 trials activate a
+proxy and 1107 chunks begin in-flight rescue. No newly assigned B$'$ chunk
+completes, and no trial establishes sustained new B$'$ use across phases.
+The current result therefore demonstrates rescue of stalled work followed
+by adaptive service, not restoration of healthy dual-plane throughput.
+A no-proxy timeout remains a valid execution outcome.
+
+The first formal \texttt{canary-service-v3} validation is preserved separately:
+580 attempts, 530 with valid execution/replay and 50 infrastructure errors
+caused by disk quota. In the quarter-capacity cohort, all 60 executions are
+valid but only 42/60 detect every affected direction below 100~ms; 18 miss
+a direction. Counting only the first alarm would conceal these misses.
+Healthy queueing inflated the canary completion reference. v4 adds whole-path
+receiver spacing after development showed that an isolated canary train was
+confounded by QP interleaving. Four old misses are development regressions
+only; the new matrix uses disjoint input seeds and a fresh frozen build.
+The first validation is never relabeled as a pass or pooled into the new 640.
+
+The historical standalone UDP observer achieves 400/400 timely faults under
+its own representative-probe envelope, but its 75.4-ms worst condition p95,
+probe costs and eight-path traffic model are different. Its earlier low-budget
+misses, reordering false alarms and management-delay failures remain in
+Appendix~\ref{app:historical-udp}. Those results motivate the new design;
+they are neither its baselines nor additional trials in its denominator.
